Package: surfacepro7-camera
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Tim Heyne <113726264+Celestial0579@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/Celestial0579/surfacepro7-camera-ir
Depends: dkms, v4l2loopback-dkms, python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-glib-2.0, gir1.2-gstreamer-1.0, gstreamer1.0-tools, gstreamer1.0-plugins-base, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, gstreamer1.0-libcamera, libcamera-ipa, systemd, udev, curl, msitools
Recommends: v4l-utils
Conflicts: v4l2-relayd
Description: Front and rear cameras for the Microsoft Surface Pro 7
 Makes the Surface Pro 7 front (OV5693) and rear (OV8865) cameras usable
 as ordinary webcams "Surface Camera Front" and "Surface Camera Back".
 .
 Contains the out-of-tree Intel IPU4P ISP and sensor drivers (built with
 DKMS), a boot service that loads them with the ISP's IOMMU group in
 identity mode, and sp7-camerad, an unprivileged, sandboxed daemon that
 starts a camera only while an application uses it. libcamera runs in a
 short-lived child process per session.
 .
 The Microsoft-signed ISP firmware is not included; install it with
 "sudo sp7-camera-firmware" (downloads and verifies it).
